Third-party assets

Avatars (core/avatar/make-avatar.py) are made with models it downloads the
first time, into ~/.cache/notchd/models; notchd doesn't ship them:
  - Depth Anything V2 Small (onnx-community/depth-anything-v2-small),
    Apache License 2.0. Its Base and Large models are not, and aren't used.
  - MediaPipe's selfie_multiclass_256x256 and face_landmarker models,
    Apache License 2.0, Copyright Google LLC.

core/modules/claude.svg is the Claude logo, a trademark of Anthropic, shown
to identify the claude module's integration with Claude Code. The file is
the one Omarchy ships (shell/plugins/agents/assets/claude.svg).
